KikasaTrialQuestLine: {
	// QuestCategory: Kikasa · The Sinking Feast
	// TrackerWaiting: Not seated yet—go invite it, or wait a while
	// TrackerFighting: "{0}: {1:0%}"
	// TrackerBrief: Next course: {0}
	// BossRushTargetName: A Table Full of Guests
	// EventActiveFormat: "{0}: In progress"
	// Trial_0: Soft First Course
	// Trial_1: Night-Staring Eye
	// Trial_2: Foul Soil Morsels
	// Trial_3: Festering Depths
	// Trial_4: Sweet Nectar and Stubborn Hooves
	// Trial_5: Old Bones at the Gate
	// Trial_6: Motley God-Gel
	// Trial_7: Flesh Across the Path
	// Trial_8: Winged Pink Gel
	// Trial_9: Golden Drool in Rotten Sand
	// Trial_10: Three Tastes of Iron
	// Trial_11: Crimson Bloom of the Jungle
	// Trial_12: Crystal-Shelled Morsel
	// Trial_13: Temple Boulder
	// Trial_14: Wave-Stirring Winged Boar
	// Trial_15: Nocturnal Radiance
	// Trial_16: Chanting at the Portal
	// Trial_17: Moonback Reflection
	// Trial_18: Kinfolk at the Table
	// Trial_19: Ancient Acid-Bather
	// Trial_20: Void Serpent Beyond
	// Trial_21: Unquenched Blazing Plume
	// Trial_22: Peak Iron and Peak Flame
	// Trial_23: The Full Table Feast
	/* TrialSummary_0:
		'''
		Something soft wobbles at the foot of the hills, blue and endless
		The lake has never tasted gel—it wants to know what the bite sounds like
		Lure it under the umbrella, never mind the stickiness
		If it melts, call it soup
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_1:
		'''
		An eye stares at people in the night, quite rudely
		The lake wrinkles whenever it catches that stare—it makes the ribs itch
		Go press that gaze into the water
		Things that watch all learn to close their eyes eventually
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_2:
		'''
		Things come burrowing out of the foul soil—one long, or one wet lump of brain
		Both taste of rot; the lake isn't picky, take whichever crosses your path
		Don't gather the pieces, let them flow in on their own
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_3:
		'''
		A rotten thought festers underground, or a nest of blood-boring worms
		One sniff downwind tells you: spoiled
		The lake says spoiled is still a flavor—serve it
		Keep your gloves on, that juice clings
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_4:
		'''
		A jar of sweetness in the jungle, a stubborn head out in the snow
		Pick one to bring—the lake is open to both tastes today
		The sweet one stings, the stubborn one stomps
		Either way, don't come back empty-handed
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_5:
		'''
		Old bones hang at the dungeon door, addicted to keeping watch
		Bones never soak soft, the lake knows—it just wants to hear the crack
		End his vigil; keep the key for yourself
		Bone dregs settle nicely, good for paving
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_6:
		'''
		A heap of gel calls itself a god, purple and black stirred together
		The lake never lacks water—what it lacks is a mouthful this big
		Lay it flat, see what it really melts into
		Don't drink; that isn't for you
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_7:
		'''
		A wall of flesh stands stacked across hell, blocking everyone's road
		Something hot—just the thing to cool the lake's temper
		Pierce it, and the world will change—that's not on you
		The canopy stops sparks, go without worry
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_8:
		'''
		A pink smear hangs over the Hallow, flying with a crystal guard
		The lake has tasted grounded gel; never the flying kind
		Drag her down, crystals and all
		Mind the shards, they chafe the ribs
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_9:
		'''
		The bloomsand serpent is back, its red blooms festered into cysts
		Don't step in the golden puddles, that is its drool
		The lake takes every flavor, it just hates what this one did to the sand
		Go, invite it to the bottom, and shake the umbrella clean after
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_10:
		'''
		Someone forged three iron things: a chain, two lamps, a frame of bones
		Iron never soaks through; steep it forever and it still tastes of rust
		Not the lake's favorite, but a feast can't lack these three courses
		One at a time—don't let them all wake on the same night
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_11:
		'''
		Deep in the jungle a great bloom smolders, red, asleep
		Few who wake her come back whole
		The lake wants her sap; it colors the water just right
		Vines on the umbrella? Cut them, no courtesy needed
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_12:
		'''
		A big shrimp nests under the beach, dressed in crystal shell, and it molts
		When its claw snaps, the water cracks, heard half a sea away
		The lake has craved this springy bite for ages, go and send the invitation
		The shell it sheds on its own, the punch you dodge on your own
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_13:
		'''
		A stone one squats in the temple—blockheaded, fond of hopping
		Stone sinks fastest; the lake's collection is short exactly one
		Break its workings and bring the shell whole
		The splash it throws up is your reward
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_14:
		'''
		A pig out at sea grew wings and dares to stir up waves
		The lake can't stand it: water's temper is not a pig's to wield
		Press it back into the water—which water, you decide
		The lake provides the bait; you dig the worm
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_15:
		'''
		A glowing one flies the Hallow at night, her temper tied to the sun
		The lake cannot hold her image—too bright for the surface to keep
		Go by night; knead that light dim and bring it back
		Provoke her at noon and the consequences are yours to keep
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_16:
		'''
		A chanter stands at the dungeon door, chanting the sky half-open
		The lake doesn't understand scripture—only that he means to let something in
		Interrupt him; let the rite rot half-finished
		If his beads drop, leave them—the lake takes no counterfeits
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_17:
		'''
		The one behind the moon has come down, covered in eyes
		Whatever falls from the sky is only a reflection once it's in the lake
		Go collect the reflection's original
		The moon will be lovely that night—watch it once for me
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_18:
		'''
		A patched-up soul drifts in the dungeon's depths, mended over centuries
		Even the ghosts steeping in the lake shrink into the ribs at the sight of it
		Killing your own kind is an ugly phrase—call it sharing a table
		After this order the umbrella gets crowded; bear with it
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_19:
		'''
		An old thing lies pressed under the Sulphurous Sea, sour in scale and temper
		The lake and he go way back; neither respects the other's water
		Deliver a message: the table is set, and he is invited to sink
		He bites, and his teeth are still good—take care
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_20:
		'''
		A long worm circles beyond the sky, and the stars keep out of its way
		It has swallowed gods; the lake wonders what god tastes like
		Make it dive into water it should never have entered
		The shell is yours, the meat belongs to the lake
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_21:
		'''
		Across the jungle they keep a ball of fire, burning who knows how long
		Fire and the lake are old rivals; time to settle it
		Press that blaze out—the lake will pour the last ladle itself
		Wet feathers don't fly; leave not one
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_22:
		'''
		The last two tables open together: one all iron, one only fire
		A craftsman's pride and a witch's obsession—the lake wants to watch both settle to the bottom
		Any order you like; just come to the table alive
		After this meal, the lake is about full
		''' */
	/* TrialSummary_23:
		'''
		They have all come back, or the old one in the abyss has woken
		A full table at last—the lake's water rose just from waiting
		You only mind the umbrella; take them one by one
		When this feast is done, the rain stops
		''' */
}

KikasaText: {
	KikasaServantPlayer: {
		// ServantUnknown: You can't command it yet
		// AutoEvictFormat: Seats full — {0} steps down, {1} takes the seat
	}

	KikasaUIText: {
		// AffinityFlame: Flame
		// AffinityNightmare: Nightmare
		// AffinityRain: Rain
		// AffinityWild: Any
		// AffinityArms: Arms
		// StateOut: Out
		// StateHeld: Held back
		// StateAwait: Waiting
		// LakeNotReadyLine: The lake isn't open. It will come out once you raise it
		// WispRainBlock: The ghost rain smothers any spark
		// NeedSettleLine: The lake hasn't settled yet
	}

	KikasaHud: {
		// ScrollName: Lakeheart
		// OpenTag: Click to open
		// TipWaterFormat: Water {0}%
		// TipTideHintFormat: Hold {0} to draw the waterline to your cursor
		// TipVaultFormat: Hoard {0} / {1}
		// TipWispClick: Click the flame sprout to light or draw back the fire
		// TipCooldownFormat: Cooling down · {0}%
		// TipDrownTitle: Drown
		// TipDrownHintFormat: Aim at an enemy or hold an item and press {0}
		// TipDrownReady: Ready
		// TipResetTitle: Wide Restart
		// TipResetHintFormat: Press {0} anytime to rewind nearby things a few seconds
		// TipTeleportTitle: Ghostwater Passage
		// TipTeleportHintFormat: Press {0} to slip through a pool of water to the cursor; swifter within the lake, with a shorter cooldown
		// TipThrallFormat: Thralls out {0} / {1}
		// TipHoundCountFormat: Hounds out {0} / {1}
		// TipDreamNoTalis: Only the hounds' bite counts here — talismans do not apply
		// TipSeatsHintFormat: Hold {0} for the wheel · change the lineup in the Lakeheart
		// TipSeatEmpty: Empty
		// TipTalisHint: Click to open the Lakeheart and hang talismans on the rope
	}

	KikasaServantWheelUI: {
		// WheelEmptyTitle: Empty
		// WheelEmptyDesc: Drown a boss and its shade takes an empty seat on its own; you can also seat one by hand in the Lakeheart
		// WheelEmptyStatus: Nothing here yet
		// WheelSeatFormat: Seat {0}
		// WheelStatusRecall: "[Release] Call it back"
		// WheelStatusSummon: "[Release] Call it out"
		// WheelStatusAwaitOrder: "[Release] Remember this; it comes out when the lake opens"
		// WheelCenterTitle: All Seats
		// WheelCenterDesc: If any are out, call them all back. If none are out, call them all out
		// WheelCenterCountFormat: "{0}/{1} out"
		// WheelCenterRecallAll: "[Release] Call all back"
		// WheelCenterSummonAll: "[Release] Call all out"
		// WheelCenterEmpty: No shades seated yet
		// WheelDamageFormat: Damage per shade out {0}%
		// WheelHint: "[{0}] Hold · Release to confirm · Right-click closes the wheel only, shades stay afield"
		// WheelWispName: Gold Flame
		// WheelWispDesc: Once lit, the gold flame spreads along the shore and scorches whatever it reaches
		// WheelWispIgnite: "[Release] Light it"
		// WheelWispSnuff: "[Release] Draw the fire back"
	}

	KikasaPanoramaUI: {
		// Title: Lakeheart
		// HoundTitle: Hound · Ghost Dream
		// WispTitle: Gold Flame · Ghost Fire
		// ReflectAwake: The reflection is awake
		// ReflectAsleep: The reflection is still asleep
		// InDreamLine: You are in the Ghost Dream
		// DreamReturnFormat: Press {0} again to return
		// DreamEnterKeyFormat: Hold {0} to enter the Ghost Dream
		// DreamEnterClick: Click the hound to enter the Ghost Dream
		// NeedDomainFormat: Press {0} to open the Blood Lake
		// NeedFullWater: The lake isn't full yet
		// HoundBonusFormat: Hound cap {0} · damage {1}%
		// WispBurning: Burning, scorching along the shore
		// WispIdle: Unlit; the flame waits on your word
		// WispBoil: Still burning in the rain
		// WispQuenchedLine: Being put out by Ghost Rain
		// WispBonusFormat: Burn {0}s · flame reach {1}
		// WispIgniteClick: Click the gold flame to light the ghost fire
		// WispSnuffClick: Click the gold flame to draw the fire back
		// ActionDreamTag: Enter the Dream
		// ActionIgniteTag: Ignite
		// ActionSnuffTag: Snuff
		// EdgeDreamFire: Dreamfire
		// EdgeBoilRain: Boiling Rain
		// EdgeRainNightmare: Rain-Nightmare
		// EdgeTriSeal: Three-Shade Seal
		// SeatsTitle: Three Seats
		// SeatEmptyLine: Empty — pick a shade from the list below
		// SeatPickHint: Click to pick up · right-click to remove
		// SeatPlaceHint: Click to place it here
		// SeatHeldLineFormat: Held back — hold {0} for the wheel to call it out
		// RosterTallyFormat: Codex {0} / {1}
		// RosterSeatTallyFormat: Seats {0} / {1}
		// RosterUnknown: Not drowned yet
		// RosterUnknownHintFormat: With the lake open, aim at it and press {0}
		// RosterSeatedTag: Seated
		// RosterPickHint: Click to pick up
		// NotePlacedFormat: "{0} is now seated"
		// NoteUnslottedFormat: "{0} was removed from its seat"
		// NoteNotCollected: You haven't drowned it yet
		// NotePickFirst: Pick a shade from the list below first
		// NoteArmsNoStock: No original of that weapon in the hoard, so the shade can't take shape
		// TalisTitle: Raincall Rope
		// TalisEmptyLine: An empty knot — click to open the talisman case
		// TalisNoneOwned: The talisman case is empty; craft a talisman at a workbench by the water first
		// TalisNeedUmbrella: Hold Kikasa in hand — the talismans answer only the umbrella
		// TalisSwapHint: Click to swap · drag onto another knot to relocate · right-click to take down
		// TalisHangHint: Click to hang it here
		// TalisTakeDownLabel: Take down
		// TalisAlreadyHung: It already hangs on another knot
		// TalisCurrentTag: Hanging here
		// TalisStackRule: Every hung talisman keeps working, even with its ink hidden; each drop takes one talisman's color and signature effect, leftmost first
		// TalisDragSwapHint: Release to trade knots
		// TalisDragMoveHint: Release to move it here
		// NoteFuHungFormat: 「{0}」rose onto the raincall rope
		// NoteFuTakenFormat: 「{0}」returned to the talisman case
		// VaultTitle: Lake Hoard
		// VaultCountFormat: "{0} / {1}"
		// VaultEmptyHint: Nothing here yet
		// VaultExtractHint: Click to take it back
		// VaultViewOnlyLine: The lake hasn't risen yet — you can only look
		// ArmsStockFormat: Originals ×{0}
		// ThrallLineFormat: Thrall cap {0} · convert one every {1}s
		// FooterHintFormat: Esc or {0} to close · hold an item and press {1} to sink it · hold {2} for the wheel
	}

	KikasaHudLead: {
		// DomainTitle: Raise the Blood Lake
		// DomainBody: The Blood Lake is where the umbrella does its work: storing items, drowning foes, and commanding shades all start with the lake open. Raise it and let the water climb. The tide answers you: hold the Command the Tide key (X by default) and the waterline follows your cursor.
		// DomainPrompt: Hold Kikasa and press {0}
		// SinkTitle: Sink Something
		// SinkBody: Hold an item and press the sink key to store it on the lakebed; you can reclaim it in the Lakeheart. Press the same key aiming at an enemy to push it under. A drowned boss leaves behind a shade, and you can command it to fight for you later.
		// SinkPrompt: Once the water reaches your feet, press {0} while holding an item or aiming at an enemy
		// PanoramaTitle: Open the Lakeheart
		// PanoramaBody: The Lakeheart is Kikasa's home screen: the hound and the ghost fire live up top, the three seats in the middle hold your shades, and everything you sank rests on the lakebed. The next steps all run through here.
		// PanoramaPrompt: Click the wind chime at the bottom left, or hold Kikasa and press {0}
		// WheelTitle: Call the Shades
		// WheelBody: Seated shades come out to fight on their own once the lake is open. The wheel calls them out or back one by one at any time: the fewer afield, the harder each one hits. The gold-flame sector on the wheel lights or draws back the ghost fire.
		// WheelPrompt: Hold {0} to open the wheel, then release on a seat
		// WheelNoMemory: No shades in the lake yet. Drown a boss first, or skip this step.
		// RainTitle: Mutate into Ghost Rain
		// RainBody: The Flip the Lake key (middle mouse by default) works two ways: at full water, tap it to flip the Blood Lake into ghost rain; hold it to sink into the Ghost Dream, saved for the last step. Foes slain under the ghost rain rise as umbrella thralls that fight for you.
		// RainPrompt: At full water, tap {0} to flip the lake
		// RestartTitle: Wide Restart
		// RestartBody: Press the restart key and the scene freezes into a black-and-white photograph, then washes open: nearby foes and you slide back to where you stood seconds ago, your life refills, debuffs rinse off, and nothing can touch you while it rewinds. It works outside the ghost rain too: the shutter borrows a ghost rain for that moment, and once the rewind settles the rain withdraws, leaving your domain as it was.
		// RestartPrompt: Hold the umbrella and press {0}
		// DreamTitle: Enter the Ghost Dream
		// DreamBody: At full water, hold the Flip the Lake key and the reflection in the lake pulls you into the dream. Foes there are helpless and no ranged projectile can exist; your items are sealed too, so hold left click to loose the hounds instead. Press the same key again to wake.
		// DreamPrompt: At full water, hold {0}
		// SkipBtn: Skip
		// ConfirmBtn: Got it
		// AssistBtn: Show me
		// OpenPanoramaBtn: Open it for me
		// DismissBtn: Put away
		// KeyUnbound: This step's key "{0}" isn't bound. Bind it in Settings > Controls, or click Skip.
		// AlreadyDoneNote: You've already done this one. Read on, then press Got it.
		// WaterRisingNote: Wait for the blood water to reach your feet. Water level: {0}%.
		// ResetCooldownFormat: Restart still cooling down: {0}%
		// HelpHover: Replay the umbrella tutorial
		// MutateFallbackKey: middle mouse
	}
}
